  "merged_at": "2026-11-12T00:39:03Z",
  "merge_commit_sha": "e14ad8f14073304f349fe45b9823b810c47c1983",
  "body": "Flutter stable 3.50 makes the existing SDK Material/Cupertino imports deprecated, causing Quality gate and every Strip job to fail. Migrate runtime code, tests, examples and generators to standalone UI libraries while retaining the existing material_ui 1.8.0 / cupertino_ui 1.1.4 versions and archive hashes; the SDK updates three test-support pins.\n\nUse matching standalone localization delegates. The SDK gen-l10n template still emits legacy Global* references, so a supported l10n header binds those identifiers to small standalone delegate adapters. Relative header imports survive application package renaming. A real widget regression exercises the generated convenience delegates in all four locales (legacy output fails ar/es/vi). Extend the architecture guard to reject standalone UI imports in domain code and document custom UI type migration/regeneration.\n\nThe scopes are tracked separately by canonical epic and implemented in serial commits; they integrate atomically because legacy and standalone public UI types differ. Native configuration PR #1224 remains separate and will be rebased after this prerequisite.\n\nValidation: isolated official Flutter 3.50.0 archive SHA256 verified; format/analyzer clean; full host suite 4,376 passed / 14 skipped; 29 focused guard/localization cases and docs checks passed. A fresh independent clone in a path containing spaces stays clean after pub get, gen-l10n twice and pub get. All seven current-head CI checks succeeded: Quality gate, Docs and every Strip variant (including renamed-both).\n\nFresh independent adversarial review by review_1237 found no actionable findings. Eleven independent probe executions cover actual Riverpod/Patrol text entry, modern themes/localization in all four locales, package renaming and GoRouter navigation/error rendering. Deleting generated locale files and regenerating restores committed bytes; removing only the header reproduces four failures in independent negative controls. Root inspected the actual probe sources, raw commands/results, source diff and five dependency provenance records. Postmerge QA/security and evidence-backed per-issue closure follow the merge.\n\nRefs koniz-dev/flutter-starter#1225\nRefs koniz-dev/flutter-starter#1226\nRefs koniz-dev/flutter-starter#1227\nRefs koniz-dev/flutter-starter#1228\nRefs koniz-dev/flutter-starter#1229\nRefs koniz-dev/flutter-starter#1230\nRefs koniz-dev/flutter-starter#1231\nRefs koniz-dev/flutter-starter#1232\nRefs koniz-dev/flutter-starter#1233\nRefs koniz-dev/flutter-starter#1234\nRefs koniz-dev/flutter-starter#1235\nRefs koniz-dev/flutter-starter#1236\n"
}
